Joel, Jim and I have drafted the following for HRC to say tomorrow:

thx

Mandy

Before we get started, I=92d like to take a minute to talk about the topic=
=85of emails.

I think there has been some confusion out there about my emails as Secretar=
y of State, so I want to talk about it directly.

When I was in the Senate, I used a Blackberry for both work and personal em=
ails. When I got to work as Secretary,  I wanted to do the same thing.  So =
I opted to use my personal email account -  which was permitted by the depa=
rtment -  because I thought it would be easier to carry just one device for=
 my work and for my personal emails, instead of two.

A lot of you know, I=92m not exactly a technological whiz.

Looking back, it would have been better if I had simply used a second email=
 account and carried a second phone, but at the time, this certainly didn=
=92t seem like an issue.

I sent my work emails to government employees at their government addresses=
, which meant they were immediately preserved on the system at the State De=
partment.

After I left office, when the Department asked  for all emails from former =
secretaries of state sent from their personal accounts, I responded  right =
away and we have turned over all of my work related emails,  which total ro=
ughly 55,000 printed pages.

I have also asked that the State Department make all of these emails public=
 so everyone can see them for themselves.


Mandy Grunwald
Grunwald Communications
202 973-9400<tel:202%20973-9400>


